1
00:00:13,088 --> 00:00:15,156
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

2
00:00:15,925 --> 00:00:17,365
(A beautiful, sunny sky welcomes them.)

3
00:00:17,365 --> 00:00:18,695
- Hello. - Hello.

4
00:00:18,695 --> 00:00:20,665
- CEO Song. - Hi, friend.

5
00:00:20,665 --> 00:00:21,965
(They're kicking things off in Gangnam.)

6
00:00:21,965 --> 00:00:24,175
Each of us can have a bite.

7
00:00:24,575 --> 00:00:25,635
A bite for each person?

8
00:00:25,635 --> 00:00:27,005
Kyoung Pyo, will you be okay today?

9
00:00:27,145 --> 00:00:28,905
Me? I'm feeling great.

10
00:00:29,515 --> 00:00:30,775
- You didn't get much sleep. - Eun I.

11
00:00:30,775 --> 00:00:33,245
I try my best to go to bed at 11pm these days.

12
00:00:33,245 --> 00:00:34,245
- Right. - And it works.

13
00:00:34,245 --> 00:00:35,245
(Eun I is worried about Kyoung Pyo who's tired.)

14
00:00:35,245 --> 00:00:38,185
I used to go to bed around 1am.

15
00:00:38,185 --> 00:00:40,055
I figured I had to do something,

16
00:00:40,055 --> 00:00:41,155
- so... - You must go to bed early.

17
00:00:41,155 --> 00:00:43,225
I made a habit of going to bed early.

18
00:00:43,425 --> 00:00:45,195
- It worked. - It's a habit.

19
00:00:45,195 --> 00:00:46,465
It's definitely a habit.

20
00:00:46,595 --> 00:00:48,565
- What did you order? Green plum? - Green plum.

21
00:00:48,565 --> 00:00:49,695
I see.

22
00:00:49,695 --> 00:00:50,965
You're thinking about your health.

23
00:00:51,665 --> 00:00:52,695
(Sucking)

24
00:00:53,165 --> 00:00:54,805
- Born in 1991. - Born in 1991.

25
00:00:55,035 --> 00:00:56,065
(All of a sudden?)

26
00:00:56,065 --> 00:00:57,305
- Park Sang Eun. - Director Park Sang Eun.

27
00:00:57,305 --> 00:00:58,705
- She was born in our class year. - Yes.

28
00:00:58,705 --> 00:01:00,505
Our class year is the same as the year she was born.

29
00:01:00,905 --> 00:01:02,845
If you were born in 1991, you're in your mid-30s.

30
00:01:03,015 --> 00:01:05,475
You're not considered young in the society.

31
00:01:06,845 --> 00:01:08,145
- That's so sad. - Why are you sad?

32
00:01:08,145 --> 00:01:09,615
You got older first.

33
00:01:09,855 --> 00:01:11,385
(Crying)

34
00:01:11,885 --> 00:01:13,025
I don't want to get older.

35
00:01:13,025 --> 00:01:15,025
Don't be sad. You already got old.

36
00:01:15,025 --> 00:01:16,655
We got aged earlier than her.

37
00:01:16,655 --> 00:01:17,755
You get to hear us say...

38
00:01:17,755 --> 00:01:19,295
that you're cute because you're here.

39
00:01:19,295 --> 00:01:20,565
You wouldn't hear that anywhere else.

40
00:01:20,695 --> 00:01:21,825
I came here dressed like this...

41
00:01:21,825 --> 00:01:23,535
because I wanted to look young.

42
00:01:23,665 --> 00:01:25,495
- Only you think you look young. - Right.

43
00:01:26,705 --> 00:01:28,165
While looking in the mirror, you thought,

44
00:01:28,165 --> 00:01:29,675
"I look quite sporty today."

45
00:01:29,675 --> 00:01:31,475
(My reflection in the mirror)

46
00:01:31,775 --> 00:01:32,875
When you put it that way,

47
00:01:32,875 --> 00:01:34,345
I think Seok Jin is very impressive.

48
00:01:34,505 --> 00:01:36,675
Seok Jin is practically struggling.

49
00:01:37,075 --> 00:01:38,745
He's all tied up, but...

50
00:01:38,815 --> 00:01:40,685
I hope that he will stop.

51
00:01:41,615 --> 00:01:43,555
I want him to be more natural.

52
00:01:45,385 --> 00:01:47,855
(Panting)

53
00:01:48,025 --> 00:01:49,055
It's so fascinating.

54
00:01:49,325 --> 00:01:50,995
Gosh, you startled me.

55
00:01:50,995 --> 00:01:52,025
I'm sorry.

56
00:01:52,025 --> 00:01:53,025
- What happened... - I'm late.

57
00:01:53,025 --> 00:01:54,965
- What's she doing? - No, you're not late.

58
00:01:55,325 --> 00:01:57,095
It's us who got here early.

59
00:01:57,295 --> 00:01:59,835
- BIBI. - What's the matter?

60
00:01:59,835 --> 00:02:01,305
Where did you start preparing your script?

61
00:02:01,305 --> 00:02:02,935
You must've started nearby because you aren't sweating.

62
00:02:02,935 --> 00:02:04,775
- Just three meters away? - That's right.

63
00:02:04,905 --> 00:02:06,545
BIBI, order your drink.

64
00:02:06,545 --> 00:02:07,545
Okay.

65
00:02:07,545 --> 00:02:08,545
(All Sixth Sense members arrive at work.)

66
00:02:08,905 --> 00:02:10,345
By the way,

67
00:02:10,345 --> 00:02:13,445
I think I caught a glimpse of today's guest.

68
00:02:13,445 --> 00:02:14,515
- Really? - Did you see him?

69
00:02:14,515 --> 00:02:17,055
I got a quick look since I can see the door.

70
00:02:17,055 --> 00:02:18,215
Is he big? What do you think?

71
00:02:18,215 --> 00:02:20,255
I think he's short.

72
00:02:20,255 --> 00:02:21,355
- He's short? - He's short.

73
00:02:21,925 --> 00:02:24,955
(Today's guest is short?)

74
00:02:24,955 --> 00:02:26,125
- He's short. - Was it Kwang Kyu?

75
00:02:26,525 --> 00:02:28,165
- No, he's younger than him. - Younger?

76
00:02:28,165 --> 00:02:29,365
There are two guests,

77
00:02:29,365 --> 00:02:30,835
- so I don't know about one of them. - You don't...

78
00:02:31,695 --> 00:02:33,565
usually describe Kwang Kyu by his height.

79
00:02:33,565 --> 00:02:36,775
He has such a distinct personality.

80
00:02:36,775 --> 00:02:38,875
(He's such a character.)

81
00:02:38,875 --> 00:02:40,075
You don't really describe him...

82
00:02:40,075 --> 00:02:41,705
- as short when talking about him. - Right.

83
00:02:41,705 --> 00:02:42,975
He's short,

84
00:02:42,975 --> 00:02:46,915
and I think he's someone you spend a lot of time with these days.

85
00:02:46,915 --> 00:02:48,145
It must be Heo Kyeong Hwan.

86
00:02:48,645 --> 00:02:51,355
- Is it Kyeong Hwan? - It's Kyeong Hwan again.

87
00:02:51,955 --> 00:02:53,985
- It must be Heo Kyeong Hwan. - Right?

88
00:02:54,185 --> 00:02:55,555
- Really? - Heo Kyeong Hwan.

89
00:02:55,555 --> 00:02:57,825
- He's been on this show before. - In the past...

90
00:02:57,825 --> 00:02:59,255
He's been on this show every season.

91
00:02:59,255 --> 00:03:00,525
- He's been here every season. - Yes.

92
00:03:00,695 --> 00:03:02,365
This is already my third time on the show.

93
00:03:02,695 --> 00:03:04,495
You don't need to listen to anyone else.

94
00:03:04,835 --> 00:03:06,065
Are you a regular on this show?

95
00:03:06,065 --> 00:03:08,105
I'm a seasonal regular member.

96
00:03:08,135 --> 00:03:09,135
- They're here. - Gosh.

97
00:03:09,135 --> 00:03:11,275
- Joo Woo Jae is here. - Woo Jae is here too.

98
00:03:11,275 --> 00:03:12,305
Goodness.

99
00:03:12,305 --> 00:03:13,375
The lanky one.

100
00:03:13,375 --> 00:03:14,375
- The lanky and the short-legged. - What a bunch of annoying people.

101
00:03:14,375 --> 00:03:15,875
- Hello. - Hello.

102
00:03:15,875 --> 00:03:17,245
Welcome, long legs and short legs.

103
00:03:17,245 --> 00:03:18,345
Stay by my side.

104
00:03:18,615 --> 00:03:19,615
(My precious short sister)

105
00:03:19,615 --> 00:03:20,885
It was really awkward walking over here.

106
00:03:20,885 --> 00:03:22,085
It's Woo Jae again.

107
00:03:22,615 --> 00:03:24,485
What brings you here?

108
00:03:24,485 --> 00:03:25,885
Woo Jae, Kyeong Hwan felt awkward with you.

109
00:03:25,885 --> 00:03:27,685
I haven't been on a show as a guest in a long time.

110
00:03:27,685 --> 00:03:29,385
- Kyoung Pyo. - "Rooftop," "Hangout with Yoo,"

111
00:03:29,385 --> 00:03:30,395
and "Sixth Sense."

112
00:03:30,395 --> 00:03:31,455
You're right.

113
00:03:31,725 --> 00:03:34,325
(The 3 major variety shows came together.)

114
00:03:34,325 --> 00:03:35,325
Everyone is here.

115
00:03:35,325 --> 00:03:38,065
- You're both wearing plaid. - Right. It's making me dizzy.

116
00:03:38,065 --> 00:03:39,135
It's making me dizzy.

117
00:03:39,135 --> 00:03:40,365
It's making you dizzy?

118
00:03:40,365 --> 00:03:41,735
- I feel dizzy. - How can you say that...

119
00:03:41,735 --> 00:03:42,975
when we haven't seen each other in a long time?

120
00:03:43,375 --> 00:03:45,375
This is Kyeong Hwan's third time on the show.

121
00:03:45,375 --> 00:03:47,245
On our way here, he kept telling me to trust him.

122
00:03:47,345 --> 00:03:49,345
- He is... - As if he were a regular.

123
00:03:49,605 --> 00:03:50,675
I have a good track record...

124
00:03:50,675 --> 00:03:52,315
- on this show. - Do you?

125
00:03:52,545 --> 00:03:54,185
He tends to bring in good ratings.

126
00:03:54,185 --> 00:03:55,185
Is that so?

127
00:03:55,185 --> 00:03:56,615
That's the best.

128
00:03:56,615 --> 00:03:57,885
For the record,

129
00:03:57,885 --> 00:03:59,655
I make an appearance...

130
00:03:59,655 --> 00:04:01,625
- every season. - Every season.

131
00:04:01,625 --> 00:04:03,525
I drop by to see how things are going.

132
00:04:03,925 --> 00:04:06,425
(Laughing)

133
00:04:06,495 --> 00:04:09,365
You should play along. Why aren't you reacting?

134
00:04:09,525 --> 00:04:10,795
It's not that I'm not reacting...

135
00:04:10,795 --> 00:04:11,935
He did react.

136
00:04:11,935 --> 00:04:13,835
"I can't stand looking at him. What should I do?"

137
00:04:13,965 --> 00:04:15,605
They're two people that I can't stand.

138
00:04:15,605 --> 00:04:16,675
- The two of them? - Yes.

139
00:04:16,675 --> 00:04:17,975
- One and two? - One and two.

140
00:04:17,975 --> 00:04:19,505
- You're not welcoming us at all. - I'm a seasonal regular.

141
00:04:19,505 --> 00:04:20,575
You're right.

142
00:04:20,575 --> 00:04:22,545
You're not welcoming us at all today.

143
00:04:22,775 --> 00:04:24,445
- Welcome who? - You should welcome us.

144
00:04:24,445 --> 00:04:26,415
- We're here as guests. - Why should I welcome you?

145
00:04:26,415 --> 00:04:28,315
You're not exactly guests.

146
00:04:28,315 --> 00:04:30,085
- But it's my first time here. - You're like family.

147
00:04:30,085 --> 00:04:31,755
Is that so?

148
00:04:31,755 --> 00:04:33,385
- Welcome! - You're being difficult.

149
00:04:33,385 --> 00:04:34,985
Welcome!

150
00:04:34,985 --> 00:04:37,225
(He finally got them to welcome him.)

151
00:04:37,225 --> 00:04:39,095
- Welcome. - I'm sorry.

152
00:04:39,095 --> 00:04:40,265
If you're going to treat me like this,

153
00:04:40,265 --> 00:04:42,425
- BIBI is saving his face. - you shouldn't have invited me.

154
00:04:42,425 --> 00:04:44,795
- BIBI is saving his face. - BIBI is saving his face.

155
00:04:44,795 --> 00:04:46,165
When he said that it was his first time here,

156
00:04:46,165 --> 00:04:48,365
Jae Seok said carelessly, "Is that so?"

157
00:04:48,835 --> 00:04:50,835
- "Oh, really?" - That's what he said.

158
00:04:50,835 --> 00:04:52,335
(You're always welcome here.)

159
00:04:52,335 --> 00:04:54,575
- Let's look at today's theme. - B-Side.

160
00:04:54,945 --> 00:04:57,315
Today's theme is Korean Food,

161
00:04:57,315 --> 00:04:59,745
That's Not How It's Done. No, No, No!

162
00:04:59,745 --> 00:05:01,745
- Please say it once. - Where should I look?

163
00:05:04,915 --> 00:05:06,925
Korean Food, That's Not How It's Done. No, No, No!

164
00:05:06,925 --> 00:05:07,925
That's nice.

165
00:05:07,925 --> 00:05:09,155
(Impressed)

166
00:05:09,485 --> 00:05:11,725
I get to see it in person.

167
00:05:11,725 --> 00:05:12,725
You've never seen it before?

168
00:05:12,725 --> 00:05:13,825
- I got to see it in person. - That's good.

169
00:05:13,825 --> 00:05:15,195
It's totally raw.

170
00:05:15,195 --> 00:05:17,195
- It's live. - Live.

171
00:05:17,365 --> 00:05:20,365
(Happy BIBI)

172
00:05:20,665 --> 00:05:22,735
These are clues for each location.

173
00:05:22,735 --> 00:05:23,735
Right.

174
00:05:23,735 --> 00:05:24,735
(Today's clues are revealed.)

175
00:05:24,735 --> 00:05:26,305
The first location.

176
00:05:27,005 --> 00:05:28,205
(First location: On-site reaction hint)

177
00:05:28,205 --> 00:05:30,675
Oh, my. It's so cute.

178
00:05:30,845 --> 00:05:32,445
It's so precious.

179
00:05:32,745 --> 00:05:33,745
"Oh, my. It's so cute."

180
00:05:33,745 --> 00:05:35,745
- "It's so precious?" - The voice creeped me out.

181
00:05:36,045 --> 00:05:37,415
It's Korean food...

182
00:05:37,415 --> 00:05:39,755
- that's cute? - That's Not How It's Done.

183
00:05:39,755 --> 00:05:41,225
(Today's theme: Korean Food, That's Not How It's Done.)

184
00:05:41,225 --> 00:05:42,725
It's Korean food, but with a bit of a twist.

185
00:05:42,725 --> 00:05:43,755
It must be songpyeon.

186
00:05:44,095 --> 00:05:45,355
- Songpyeon? - Why songpyeon?

187
00:05:45,355 --> 00:05:46,495
- It's cute... - Right.

188
00:05:46,495 --> 00:05:47,525
and precious.

189
00:05:47,525 --> 00:05:49,965
That's a simple-minded guess.

190
00:05:51,595 --> 00:05:55,305
(Is that the best you can do?)

191
00:05:55,705 --> 00:05:57,535
That's a simple-minded guess.

192
00:05:57,535 --> 00:05:58,575
Jae Seok.

193
00:05:59,035 --> 00:06:01,875
- What if I'm right? - You won't get it right.

194
00:06:01,875 --> 00:06:04,615
- "What if I'm right?" - That's a simple-minded guess.

195
00:06:04,975 --> 00:06:06,515
Here's the second B-Side.

196
00:06:07,215 --> 00:06:10,315
(Second location: On-site reaction hint)

197
00:06:10,315 --> 00:06:12,585
- It sounds like something sizzling. - How many times will you milk that?

198
00:06:12,815 --> 00:06:14,355
It's got many flavors.

199
00:06:14,985 --> 00:06:16,455
"How many times will you milk that?"

200
00:06:16,455 --> 00:06:17,755
"It's got many flavors."

201
00:06:17,855 --> 00:06:19,995
Was that the sound of grinding or frying something?

202
00:06:21,965 --> 00:06:26,705
(Was that something being ground or something frying?)

203
00:06:27,105 --> 00:06:28,835
"How many times will you milk that?"

204
00:06:29,205 --> 00:06:30,905
Isn't it Kyeong Hwan who keeps milking the same joke?

205
00:06:32,405 --> 00:06:33,575
(Reusing his catchphrase endlessly)

206
00:06:33,575 --> 00:06:34,875
- His catchphrase... - His catchphrase.

207
00:06:34,875 --> 00:06:36,375
He really milks his catchphrases.

208
00:06:36,375 --> 00:06:37,915
I forgot my catchphrases.

209
00:06:39,075 --> 00:06:40,785
This is the third and last B-Side.

210
00:06:42,085 --> 00:06:44,655
I really can't figure out the inside.

211
00:06:45,055 --> 00:06:48,825
- He can't figure out the inside. - Isn't it unbalanced?

212
00:06:50,455 --> 00:06:51,655
It must be dumplings.

213
00:06:51,925 --> 00:06:53,025
- What? - How so?

214
00:06:53,495 --> 00:06:54,725
"I really can't figure out the inside."

215
00:06:54,725 --> 00:06:55,765
A thing that has something inside?

216
00:06:55,765 --> 00:06:58,235
Maybe it's something that's not normally inside dumplings.

217
00:06:58,235 --> 00:06:59,905
- It's not ordinary dumplings? - It's not the usual filling?

218
00:07:00,965 --> 00:07:02,765
Are you going to figure everything out right here?

219
00:07:03,735 --> 00:07:04,805
(Discouraged)

220
00:07:04,805 --> 00:07:05,935
I won't.

221
00:07:07,545 --> 00:07:10,045
- I'll hold back. - You're so simple-minded.

222
00:07:10,375 --> 00:07:13,075
- You're being too hasty. - Am I figuring everything out?

223
00:07:13,245 --> 00:07:15,485
(Don't misunderstand. They're close friends.)

224
00:07:15,485 --> 00:07:17,955
BIBI is also good at guessing,

225
00:07:18,085 --> 00:07:19,755
- but now that Woo Jae is here... - Right.

226
00:07:19,755 --> 00:07:21,955
- Woo Jae will... - He has good intuition.

227
00:07:21,955 --> 00:07:24,495
I've watched Sixth Sense a lot.

228
00:07:24,695 --> 00:07:27,595
Does it bother you when a guest tries hard to figure things out?

229
00:07:28,095 --> 00:07:29,665
No, not at all.

230
00:07:29,665 --> 00:07:30,865
Then I'll do my best.

231
00:07:30,865 --> 00:07:32,695
What if you end up getting it wrong?

232
00:07:33,365 --> 00:07:35,365
- I think I can get this right. - Really?

233
00:07:35,365 --> 00:07:37,035
While watching the show on TV,

234
00:07:37,405 --> 00:07:38,535
my guesses were accurate.

235
00:07:38,535 --> 00:07:40,845
(Doubtful)

236
00:07:40,975 --> 00:07:42,805
Let's see what happens this week.

237
00:07:43,315 --> 00:07:44,545
- No. - Kyeong Hwan is the ratings fairy,

238
00:07:44,545 --> 00:07:45,815
and Woo Jae is the ratings curse.

239
00:07:45,815 --> 00:07:46,915
Really?

240
00:07:46,915 --> 00:07:49,015
- One of them wins after a fight. - We'll balance each other.

241
00:07:49,245 --> 00:07:50,655
Shall we get going?

242
00:07:50,655 --> 00:07:52,115
Let's move.

243
00:07:54,325 --> 00:07:56,085
Unfortunately...

244
00:07:56,525 --> 00:07:58,495
I didn't want to do this either.

245
00:07:59,155 --> 00:08:01,025
I've lived in this neighborhood for two years.

246
00:08:01,025 --> 00:08:02,365
- Where? - On this alley.

247
00:08:02,465 --> 00:08:04,035
- Here? - When did you live here?

248
00:08:04,195 --> 00:08:05,565
About 3 or 4 years ago.

249
00:08:05,565 --> 00:08:06,905
- Really? - Yes.

250
00:08:07,405 --> 00:08:08,905
- Is this the place? - What?

251
00:08:09,735 --> 00:08:10,805
You don't know this place, right?

252
00:08:10,935 --> 00:08:13,245
- Is this the place? - Woo Jae used to live...

253
00:08:13,245 --> 00:08:14,475
- Really? - around here.

254
00:08:14,675 --> 00:08:15,805
(This is today's first restaurant.)

255
00:08:15,805 --> 00:08:17,375
- "Small Table." - What?

256
00:08:17,375 --> 00:08:19,445
- What? - "Small Table?"

257
00:08:19,445 --> 00:08:20,645
"Small Table."

258
00:08:20,785 --> 00:08:22,185
Isn't this the place where they said it was cute?

259
00:08:22,485 --> 00:08:24,455
- "It's so cute." - Yes. "It's so precious."

260
00:08:24,455 --> 00:08:26,015
